The original loop recomputes `fields.size()` and indexes `fields[i]` on every pass. This version gets the vector's start and end pointers once and walks a raw pointer from one to the other. The search order is unchanged, so it still returns the first field whose number matches.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    Field* it = fields.data();
    Field* const end = it + fields.size();
    for (; it != end; ++it)
    {
        if (it->GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return it;
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```